{"source": "talk.mp4", "duration_s": 59.7, "language": "en", "segments": [{"i": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 7.22, "text": "The keeper of the north light had not spoken to anyone in eleven days and the silence had become a kind of company to him."}, {"i": 1, "start": 7.25, "end": 13.59, "text": "The supply boat was late, the radio was silent, and the fog had swallowed the whole island in a cold grey blanket."}, {"i": 2, "start": 13.62, "end": 18.81, "text": "On the twelfth night the radio crackled and a small clear voice asked for help in the dark."}, {"i": 3, "start": 18.84, "end": 24.6, "text": "It said it was lost out on the water and that it could just see a light through the fog."}, {"i": 4, "start": 24.63, "end": 30.11, "text": "So the keeper climbed the tower and turned the great lamp by hand, slow and steady, all night long."}, {"i": 5, "start": 30.14, "end": 35.33, "text": "He told the voice to row toward the light and to count every flash out loud with him."}, {"i": 6, "start": 35.36, "end": 39.96, "text": "For an hour they counted together, one, two, three, four, over and over in the cold."}, {"i": 7, "start": 39.99, "end": 45.18, "text": "Then the voice went quiet, and the keeper waited by the radio until the fog began to lift."}, {"i": 8, "start": 45.21, "end": 50.69, "text": "At dawn there was no boat on the water and nobody on the rocks below the tower at all."}, {"i": 9, "start": 50.72, "end": 55.9, "text": "But in the logbook, written in a child's careful hand, someone had left a single word for him."}, {"i": 10, "start": 55.93, "end": 59.67, "text": "Thanks, it said, and the keeper never found out who had written it."}], "words": [{"w": "The", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.26, "seg": 0}, {"w": "keeper", "start": 0.29, "end": 0.55, "seg": 0}, {"w": "of", "start": 0.58, "end": 0.84, "seg": 0}, {"w": "the", "start": 0.87, "end": 1.13, "seg": 0}, {"w": "north", "start": 1.16, "end": 1.42, "seg": 0}, {"w": "light", "start": 1.45, "end": 1.71, "seg": 0}, {"w": "had"